{
  "id": "h614",
  "number": 614,
  "title": "Sound the Battle Cry",
  "artist": "Traditional",
  "key": "G",
  "lyrics": [
    "Verse 1:",
    "[G]Sound the battle cry, [C]See! the [G]foe is nigh;",
    "[D]Raise [G]the [D]standard high [A7]For the [D]Lord;",
    "[G]Gird your armor on, [C]Stand firm, [G]every one,",
    "Rest your [Em]cause upon His [G]holy word.",
    "",
    "Refrain:",
    "[G]Rouse, then soldiers! [D7]rally round the [G]banner!",
    "[B]Ready, [Em]steady, [A7]pass the word [D]along;",
    "[G]Onward, forward, [D7]shout aloud [G]hosanna!",
    "[G]Christ is [Em]Captain of the [G]mighty throng.",
    "",
    "Verse 2:",
    "Strong to meet the foe,",
    "Marching on we go,",
    "While our cause we know",
    "Must prevail;",
    "Shield and banner bright,",
    "Gleaming in the light,",
    "Battling for the right,",
    "We ne'er can fail.",
    "",
    "Verse 3:",
    "O Thou God of all,",
    "Hear us when we call,",
    "Help us, one and all,",
    "By Thy grace;",
    "When the battle's done,",
    "And the victory won,",
    "May we wear the crown",
    "Before Thy face."
  ],
